        rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Source and data traceability: 88/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Credit: all five dataset files are SHA-256-pinned and verified fail-closed at runtime (`verify_dataset_integrity` L158-185, `load_pass3_reference` L191-208, `EXPECTED_PASS3_SHA256` L114); the new JSON carries per-row provenance flags (literature / literature-approx / literature-qualitative / theory-exact / theory-null / model) and `doi_verified_offline: false` (JSON L9); `pass3_citations.bib` and the README addendum list all seven new references and state the caveats; the header docstring (L1-80) lists all ten sources with DOIs. Deductions: the Schoen (1970) DOI 10.1063/1.1665587 (JSON L19, carried from v2) is a J. Math. Phys. DOI, not NASA TN D-5541 (which has none; NTRS 19700020472) — kept and flagged because it could not be verified offline (-2); all seven Pass 3 DOIs were recalled from memory and are unverified (-2); the 12-species table has no per-row provenance and is effectively synthetic (-2). Net -6 from v2." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
